weeks@astroatc.UUCP (Pat Weeks) writes:

>	OK, I'm getting better but I have a question to ask you true hackers
>out there?
>
>1)  How in the heck do you create Holy Water besides the obvious altar method.
>I understand there's a way involving fountains, but I'm a bit clueless at this
>point...
SPOILERS!


Without an altar, the only way to make holy water is to polymorph blessed
potions and hope one becomes a potion of water.
Holy water can also be obtained by wishing for it. Other than that, you just
have to hope you find some in a shop or on the floor of the dungeon.

Once you have a potion of holy water, you can make more by dipping uncursed
potions of water in the potion of holy water. You can obtain uncursed potions
of water by dipping other potions in a fountain (or pool while wearing water-
walking boots) or by zapping them with a wand of cancellation.

>2)  Are some fountains filled with cursed, regular, or holy water?  What's
>	the story.  Holy water is so ultimately useful and I wanna know more 
>	about it!

No. It's just that sometimes dipping in a fountain curses or uncurses objects.
It has nothing to do with holy/unholy water.

